<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-23472] Fix flaky JavaLoggerTest</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-23472</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Field `JavaLogger#inited` is used for DCL pattern while initializing logger. The test checks `JavaLogger#cfg` to be non-null that is actually null if run test multiple times. There is no guarantee for the `cfg` field to be initialized with the DCL.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Need to investigate how to refactor JavaLogger to make test green.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ci2.ignite.apache.org/buildConfiguration/IgniteTests24Java8_RunAll/8117150?buildTab=tests&amp;amp;suite=org.apache.ignite.testsuites.IgniteLoggingSelfTestSuite%3A+&amp;amp;package=org.apache.ignite.logger.java&amp;amp;class=JavaLoggerTest&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://ci2.ignite.apache.org/buildConfiguration/IgniteTests24Java8_RunAll/8117150?buildTab=tests&amp;amp;suite=org.apache.ignite.testsuites.IgniteLoggingSelfTestSuite%3A+&amp;amp;package=org.apache.ignite.logger.java&amp;amp;class=JavaLoggerTest&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
